</head>
<body>

  <div class="br-shell">

    <div class="print-hint screen-only">
      <span class="accent">Print to PDF &rarr;</span>
      Press <kbd>&#8984; P</kbd> (or <kbd>Ctrl + P</kbd>). Choose <strong>Save as PDF</strong>. Margins <strong>None</strong>. Background graphics <strong>on</strong>.
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
         PAGE 1 · Cover · Positioning · What this is
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="br-page">
      <p class="br-cover-eyebrow">A briefing for school heads</p>
      <h1 class="br-wordmark">Cultivated <span class="ai">AI</span></h1>
      <p class="br-verb"><span class="grow">Grow</span>, don't <span class="chase">Chase</span>.</p>

      <div class="br-positioning">
        <p>We train <span class="who">your teachers</span> to <span class="what">shape AI in their classrooms</span>, before <span class="against">vendors and students</span> shape it for them.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="br-prose" style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">
        <p>Just buying licences for the AI tools your edtech vendor pitched will not lead to <em>meaningful AI adoption</em> in the classroom. Your teachers have to understand how to approach AI. Meanwhile, your students are already there. Most of your faculty isn't.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="br-example">
        <p class="label">For example</p>
        <p>Two in three teens use AI chatbots. Almost <em>half</em> of those who used AI for schoolwork did it without telling a teacher. The school's policy will not be the first thing to govern this. The teacher's judgment will.</p>
      </div>

      <span class="br-section-label">What <span class="accent">Cultivated AI for Schools</span> is</span>
      <div class="br-prose">
        <p>Cultivated AI for Schools is a <em>12-hour workshop</em> where fifteen teachers from your school learn to place AI in the context of their daily classroom work. Each teacher walks away with a <em>personalised 90-day classroom plan</em>. The cohort co-authors a <em>school AI policy draft</em>, defensible to your board and to your parents. Critically, they will learn to think clearly about AI as the tools change every quarter.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="br-footer">
        <span class="brand">Cultivated AI &middot; <em>For Schools</em></span>
        <span class="num">Page 1 of 6 &middot; Cover</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
         PAGE 2 · The disciplines + the four stages
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="br-page">
      <p class="br-eyebrow">The discipline &middot; why it works</p>
      <h2 class="br-page-title">The schools winning learned to <em>think clearly</em>.</h2>
      <p class="br-page-sub">About AI, in the context of <strong>their own</strong> faculty, students, and parents. With principles that hold up as the tools change every quarter.</p>

      <div class="br-disciplines">
        <div class="br-discipline">
          <p class="d-num">01</p>
          <p class="d-title"><em>Pilot</em>, don't mandate.</p>
          <p class="d-body">8&ndash;50 schools. Measured. Then expanded. South Australia is the textbook case.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="br-discipline">
          <p class="d-num">02</p>
          <p class="d-title"><em>Train</em> teachers first.</p>
          <p class="d-body">Before the tool. Not after. The 68% with no training is not an accident.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="br-discipline">
          <p class="d-num">03</p>
          <p class="d-title"><em>Write</em> policy. Tell parents.</p>
          <p class="d-body">96% of elementary families have heard nothing from their school. Fix that first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="br-discipline">
          <p class="d-num">04</p>
          <p class="d-title">Design for student <em>agency</em>.</p>
          <p class="d-body">Estonia's app refuses direct answers. The PNAS "Tutor mode" neutralised the harm.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="br-discipline" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;">
          <p class="d-num">05</p>
          <p class="d-title"><em>Augment</em> teachers, never replace.</p>
          <p class="d-body">Aila pauses to keep the teacher in the driving seat. Alpha School's "no teachers" claim is collapsing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <span class="br-section-label">The four <span class="accent">stages</span> of Cultivated AI for Schools</span>
      <ul class="br-stages-list">
        <li class="br-stage-row s1">
          <span class="br-stage-num">Stage 1</span>
          <span class="br-stage-name">Approach</span>
          <span class="br-stage-tag">Fifteen principles teachers walk in repeating. <em>The teacher stops chasing tools and starts thinking clearly about them.</em></span>
        </li>
        <li class="br-stage-row s2">
          <span class="br-stage-num">Stage 2</span>
          <span class="br-stage-name">Practice</span>
          <span class="br-stage-tag">Build classroom playbooks &mdash; in your subject, in your voice, on your timetable. <em>The technical term is agentic skills.</em></span>
        </li>
        <li class="br-stage-row s3">
          <span class="br-stage-num">Stage 3</span>
          <span class="br-stage-name">Policy</span>
          <span class="br-stage-tag">Draft your school's own AI policy. Run incident drills. <em>Defensible to your board, to your parents, to the regulator.</em></span>
        </li>
        <li class="br-stage-row s4">
          <span class="br-stage-num">Stage 4</span>
          <span class="br-stage-name">Studio</span>
          <span class="br-stage-tag">Synthetic environments for differentiation, IEPs, parent conferences, deepfake drills. <em>Things schools could not rehearse before AI.</em></span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="br-footer">
        <span class="brand">Cultivated AI &middot; <em>For Schools</em></span>
        <span class="num">Page 2 of 6 &middot; The discipline</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
         PAGE 3 · Anjali · the four stages in one teacher's practice
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="br-page">
      <p class="br-eyebrow">An example</p>
      <h2 class="br-page-title">Meet <em>Anjali</em>.</h2>

      <p class="br-anjali-intro">Anjali teaches middle-school English at a 1,200-student CBSE school. Three Year 8 sets, one Year 9 elective, three SEN students across her classes. Twelve years in. <em>The AI conversation in her staff room used to be panic. Now it's practice.</em></p>

      <div class="br-anjali-stages">
        <div class="br-anjali-stage s1">
          <div class="ps-head"><span class="ps-num">Stage 1</span><h3>Approach &mdash; how Anjali now thinks.</h3></div>
          <p class="lede">Anjali has internalised four principles she uses on every AI question that lands in her classroom. <em>She stopped asking which tool to buy; she started asking how to think.</em></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Plan for the AI of <em>next term</em></li>
            <li>Ask AI to ask <em>you</em> the questions</li>
            <li>Cross-check answers with another model</li>
            <li>Design for the <em>process</em>, not the output</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="br-anjali-stage s2">
          <div class="ps-head"><span class="ps-num">Stage 2</span><h3>Practice &mdash; her playbooks now run as classroom AI.</h3></div>
          <p class="lede">What was between Anjali's ears for a decade now runs as agentic skills &mdash; in her voice, on her timetable, for her three sets. These are her first five.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Reading-level rewriter</li>
            <li>Socratic essay-feedback partner</li>
            <li>Parent-conference brief composer</li>
            <li>IEP-aware worksheet generator</li>
            <li>Citation-and-source integrity checker</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="br-anjali-stage s3">
          <div class="ps-head"><span class="ps-num">Stage 3</span><h3>Policy &mdash; the cohort co-authored what 96% of families haven't seen.</h3></div>
          <p class="lede">Five sections, defensible to the board, the parents, and the regulator. Anjali did not write all of it; the cohort did, together.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>What students may use AI for</li>
            <li>How AI use must be cited</li>
            <li>Deepfake / harassment incident protocol</li>
            <li>What parents will be told</li>
            <li>What the school will <em>never</em> do</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="br-anjali-stage s4">
          <div class="ps-head"><span class="ps-num">Stage 4</span><h3>Studio &mdash; she rehearses what hasn't happened yet.</h3></div>
          <p class="lede">Synthetic AI environments her school could not rehearse before. For Anjali, these are unlocks that simply weren't possible.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Parent-conference rehearsals</li>
            <li>Deepfake-incident response drill</li>
            <li>Differentiation simulations</li>
            <li>New-teacher onboarding scenarios</li>
            <li>SEN review dry-runs</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="br-footer">
        <span class="brand">Cultivated AI &middot; <em>For Schools</em></span>
        <span class="num">Page 3 of 6 &middot; Anjali</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
         PAGE 4 · Three positive case studies
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="br-page">
      <p class="br-eyebrow">Some case studies</p>
      <h2 class="br-page-title">When the leadership sets a <em>public standard</em>.</h2>

      <div class="br-paired-cases">
        <div class="br-paired-case estonia">
          <p class="case-eyebrow">National rollout &middot; Sept 2025</p>
          <h3 class="case-name">Estonia &middot; AI Leap</h3>
          <div class="case-stat">
            <p class="num">154 schools</p>
            <p class="label">All upper-secondary. ChatGPT Edu + Gemini, free for every teacher. <em>Custom Estonian-language app refuses direct answers; it scaffolds reasoning.</em> 60%+ teachers using AI weekly.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-quote">
            <p class="q">"Estonia's true leap is to learn to think with AI, <em>not instead of it</em>."</p>
            <p class="attr">Kristina Kallas, Minister of Education</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="br-paired-case sa">
          <p class="case-eyebrow">State rollout &middot; pilot &rarr; statewide</p>
          <h3 class="case-name">South Australia &middot; EdChat</h3>
          <div class="case-stat">
            <p class="num">94%</p>
            <p class="label">of student interactions related to curriculum subjects. Built with Microsoft on Azure. <em>8 schools / 1,500 students &rarr; 10K students &rarr; statewide.</em> The textbook example of pilot done right.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-quote">
            <p class="q">A federal framework first, then a phased rollout. <em>No mandate. No big bang.</em></p>
            <p class="attr">SA Department for Education</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="br-paired-case honest wide">
          <p class="case-eyebrow">The honest counter-example &middot; even the best tool isn't a strategy</p>
          <h3 class="case-name">Khanmigo &middot; Sal Khan's reckoning</h3>
          <div class="case-stat">
            <p class="num">15%</p>
            <p class="label">of students with access regularly engage with the AI tutor. <em>Free for every teacher worldwide via Microsoft. 795 districts. 2 million users.</em> The product was rebuilt in 2026 in response.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-quote">
            <p class="q">"For a lot of students, it was a non-event. They just didn't use it much. <em>Our biggest lever is investing in the human systems</em>."</p>
            <p class="attr">Sal Khan &middot; Chalkbeat, April 2026</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="br-why">
        <p class="label">Why this matters for you</p>
        <p>The most thoughtful systems on three continents made the same call. Teacher-first. Scaffolded. Phased. Even Khan, with the best-funded global tutor, came to the same conclusion: <em>the binding constraint is the human, not the model.</em></p>
      </div>

      <div class="br-footer">
        <span class="brand">Cultivated AI &middot; <em>For Schools</em></span>
        <span class="num">Page 4 of 6 &middot; Case studies</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
         PAGE 5 · Failure modes
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="br-page">
      <p class="br-eyebrow">Some failure modes</p>
      <h2 class="br-page-title">What can still <em>go wrong</em>.</h2>

      <div class="br-paired-cases">
        <div class="br-paired-case lausd">
          <p class="case-eyebrow">Vendor splurge &middot; bankruptcy</p>
          <h3 class="case-name">LAUSD &middot; "Ed"</h3>
          <div class="case-stat">
            <p class="num">$6.2M</p>
            <p class="label">contract with AllHere. ~$3M paid before launch. <em>Eight weeks later: bankruptcy. Student data routed to 8 foreign countries. CEO indicted for securities fraud. FBI raided the Superintendent's home.</em></p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-quote">
            <p class="q">Scope too broad. Vendor too small. Procurement before pedagogy.</p>
            <p class="attr">Cultivated AI assessment</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="br-paired-case korea">
          <p class="case-eyebrow">National mandate &middot; political collapse</p>
          <h3 class="case-name">South Korea &middot; AIDT</h3>
          <div class="case-stat">
            <p class="num">86%</p>
            <p class="label">of teachers and parents <em>opposed</em> the rollout. ₩1.2 trillion (~$850M) committed. Adoption fell 37% &rarr; 19% in one semester. Downgraded to "supplementary materials" in August 2025.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-quote">
            <p class="q">"Top-down mandate. No meaningful pilot. <em>No teacher consultation</em>."</p>
            <p class="attr">Failure-mode summary &middot; OECD</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="br-paired-case deepfake wide">
          <p class="case-eyebrow">The new category of incident &middot; happening in schools right now</p>
          <h3 class="case-name">The deepfake reality</h3>
          <div class="case-stat">
            <p class="num">347 / 59 / 6 mo</p>
            <p class="label">347 explicit AI images of 59 minors at <em>Lancaster Country Day, Pennsylvania</em>. The school received the tip. <em>Did not report. Police were told six months later, by a parent.</em> Westfield NJ, Almendralejo Spain, and the South Korea Telegram scandal (500+ schools, 920 victims) are the parallel stories.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-quote">
            <p class="q">40% of US students aware of deepfakes in their schools. <em>6 in 10 teachers unaware of any school policy</em> for handling them. The federal TAKE IT DOWN Act now applies.</p>
            <p class="attr">CDT, 2024 &middot; TAKE IT DOWN Act, May 2025</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="br-why">
        <p class="label">Why this matters for you</p>
        <p>The failure modes above are the default outcome when AI procurement, or AI panic, comes before AI thinking in the staff room. Stages 1 and 3 of the Cultivated AI for Schools workshop exist <em>precisely to ensure your faculty approaches AI with the clarity, and the policy, to avoid all three</em>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="br-footer">
        <span class="brand">Cultivated AI &middot; <em>For Schools</em></span>
        <span class="num">Page 5 of 6 &middot; Failure modes</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
         PAGE 6 · What we'll do · format · instructor · thesis
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <div class="br-page">
      <p class="br-eyebrow">The engagement</p>
      <h2 class="br-page-title">Exactly <em>what we'll do</em>.</h2>
      <p class="br-page-sub">A 4-stage workshop that moves your faculty from L0 / L1 to L2, with the trajectory and tools to reach L3 on their own.</p>

      <div class="br-stages-row">
        <div class="br-stage-card s1">
          <span class="br-stage-num">Stage 1</span>
          <span class="br-stage-name">Approach</span>
          <span class="br-stage-tag">15 core principles for teachers.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="br-stage-card s2">
          <span class="br-stage-num">Stage 2</span>
          <span class="br-stage-name">Practice</span>
          <span class="br-stage-tag">Build classroom playbooks.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="br-stage-card s3">
          <span class="br-stage-num">Stage 3</span>
          <span class="br-stage-name">Policy</span>
          <span class="br-stage-tag">Draft your school's own.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="br-stage-card s4">
          <span class="br-stage-num">Stage 4</span>
          <span class="br-stage-name">Studio</span>
          <span class="br-stage-tag">Differentiation. IEPs. Drills.</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="br-page-sub">Every stage is workshopped in the context of <strong>your subjects, your students, and your school's policies</strong>.</p>

      <div class="br-spec-grid">
        <div class="br-spec-row"><span class="br-spec-key">Format</span><span class="br-spec-val">12-hour workshop. <em>Six 2-hour sessions over six weeks</em>, scheduled around the school timetable.</span></div>
        <div class="br-spec-row"><span class="br-spec-key">Cohort</span><span class="br-spec-val">Up to fifteen teachers from one school. Mixed subjects, mixed seniority.</span></div>
        <div class="br-spec-row"><span class="br-spec-key">Per teacher</span><span class="br-spec-val">A personalised <em>90-day classroom plan</em>, in their subject and voice. Not a template.</span></div>
        <div class="br-spec-row"><span class="br-spec-key">Per school</span><span class="br-spec-val">A co-authored <em>AI policy draft</em> for the school, defensible to the board, the parents, and the regulator.</span></div>
      </div>

      <span class="br-section-label"><span class="accent">Conducted by</span></span>
      <div class="br-instructor">
        <h3>Shalin Shodhan</h3>
        <p>Twenty years across Pixar (six animated features, three Academy Awards), EA (<em>Spore</em>, BAFTA-winning), Lumosity, and Osmo &mdash; <em>building learning software for children</em>. Carnegie Mellon. Author of the AI curriculum <em>Talking to Machines</em>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="br-closer">
        <p>Schools that win don't <span class="strike">chase the next vendor</span>. They <em>grow the teachers they already have</em>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="br-footer">
        <span class="brand">Cultivated AI &middot; <em>For Schools</em></span>
        <span class="num">Page 6 of 6 &middot; What we will do</span>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

